    "updated_at": "2023-08-01T21:31:29Z",
    "body": "> The `BroadcastChannel` API is a cross-document messaging mechanism\r\n\r\nThe [cross-document messaging](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#web-messaging) you quoted is a link, it doesn't just mean a messaging method that can be done accross different documents, but really `Window#postMessage()`. For BroadcastChannel it's called [Broadcasting to other browsing contexts](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#broadcasting-to-other-browsing-contexts). Even `MessagePort#postMessage()` could be done in a cross-document way.\r\n\r\nSo the text in the citation is correct, only `Window.onmessage` and `SharedWorker.onconnect` will receive a non null `source` (well, ServiceWorker too, but they're defined on another spec)",
